This applies the secant iteration until the successive approximations differ by at most the tolerance $e$.

Since the population is measured in millions, a thousand individuals corresponds to a tolerance of $0.001$.

We need solve

$$f(x_4)-2=0.$$ 

Suitable Matlab code using a root-finding method is:

```matlab
f = @(x) 7*x.*exp(-x);
g = @(x) f(x) - 2;
e = 0.001;
p = 0.1;
q = 1.0;

while abs(q-p) > e
    r = q - g(q)*(q-p)/(g(q)-g(p));
    p = q;
    q = r;
end

x4 = q;
```

This gives the smaller solution

$$x_4 \approx 0.407.$$ 

Depending on the starting points, the larger solution may also be found:

$$x_4 \approx 2.578.$$
